meta {
  name: Update TACOTS recommended student status
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/forms/tacots/recommendation/{{id}}/status?status=NOT SELECTED
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  status: NOT SELECTED
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
  id: 52d738dd-0bfb-425c-a1b8-31ec3aa3e9ea
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Update TACOTS Recommended Student Status
  
  Updates the admin selection status of a TACOTS recommendation record. Used to mark a recommended student as selected, not selected, or keep in view. On status change, all related cache entries (single record and paginated lists) are invalidated.
  
  ## Authorization
  Requires `update` permission.
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Description                                |
  |-----------|--------|----------|--------------------------------------------|
  | id        | string | Yes      | UUID of the TACOTS recommendation record   |
  
  ## Query Parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type   | Required | Default        | Description / Allowed Values                          |
  |-----------|--------|----------|----------------|-------------------------------------------------------|
  | status    | string | No       | `KEEP IN VIEW` | One of: `NOT SELECTED`, `KEEP IN VIEW`, `SELECTED`    |
  
  ## Response
  
  **`200 OK`** — Returns the updated recommendation record with `id` and `adminStatus` fields.
  
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "...",
    "data": { ... },
    "meta": {
      "correlationId": "uuid-v4-string"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Errors
  
  | Status                      | Description                                             |
  |-----------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
  | `400 Bad Request`           | Invalid `id` format or unknown `status` value.          |
  | `401 Unauthorized`          | Missing or invalid authentication token.                |
  | `403 Forbidden`             | User does not have `update` permission.                 |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Unexpected server error.                                |
}
